      "side": 1,
      "message": "Previous merely reset the bundle value, and then assigned to subnode.  This keeps the original value of bundle. The reassignment was not necessary.\n\nAs far as how it behaves, it removes \"Falsy\" values from the collection, which is what you are seeing.  In the case of an object assignment, that means None.  We don\u0027t add anything to bundle that isn\u0027t either a subnode or None.  A subnode that evaluates to False would be an empty list, and it would  be correct to remove that.",
